          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-20971 utils: fix pfind work unit path buffer overflow",
        "message": "LU-20971 utils: fix pfind work unit path buffer overflow\n\nwork_unit_create() allocates PATH_MAX + 1 bytes for the path of a\nwork unit, but find_worker() gives that buffer to\nllapi_semantic_traverse() with a size of 2 * PATH_MAX, and the\ntraversal appends the name of each entry to the path in place. For\na directory whose path is longer than about PATH_MAX - NAME_MAX,\nthe worker writes past the end of the buffer, which makes glibc\nabort \"lfs find\" with \"double free or corruption\". A directory path\nlonger than PATH_MAX is also silently truncated when the work unit\nis created, while the serial traversal handles it.\n\nStore the work unit path with its exact length, and have each worker\nthread build the entry paths in a private buffer of FIND_PATH_BUFLEN\n(2 * PATH_MAX) bytes, the size of the serial traversal buffer. Use\nthe same constant in param_callback(), which gave the traversal a\nsize of 2 * PATH_MAX + 1 for a buffer of 2 * PATH_MAX bytes.\n\nTest sanity test_56Da is extended to exercise this case.\n\nFixes: 99f47b1367 (\"LU-17814 utils: implement real pfind\")\nSigned-off-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Id4bdfee4e346d401610c6e7df0496d89069b750f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
